{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789856030,"nonce":"ztw2FdjYnYFANHF+8vZr4bx+PR4=","title":"Lua: load with an explicit nil environment is read as no environment","message":"load(chunk, name, mode, nil) and loadfile(name, mode, nil) give the chunk a nil _ENV in the reference (return _ENV is nil; a global access raises), but the builtin parameters cannot tell nil from absent, so the chunk runs with the globals table (files.lua 'loadfile with env'). Needs the last parameter as Rest so absence is visible, and a chunk environment that may be nil (the env variable is Any already; index errors on it name upvalue _ENV).","files":null}]}